#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Introduction to quantum-safe cryptography {#introduction-to-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Pengenalan kepada kriptografi selamat-kuantum {#introduction-to-quantum-"
"safe-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since quantum computers represent a [distinct and potentially more powerful "
"paradigm for "
"computing](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/132/16/160902/2837574/The-"
"future-of-quantum-computing-with) than the classical computers in use today,"
" cryptographic security needs to be reassessed for a world where quantum "
"computers may <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"The rapid or exponential "
"growth, increase, or multiplication of something, typically in a biological,"
" technological, or abstract context.\">proliferate</DefinitionTooltip>, "
"enabling new cryptographic attacks that would not be possible using "
"classical computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Memandangkan komputer kuantum mewakili [paradigma pengkomputeran yang "
"tersendiri dan berpotensi lebih "
"berkuasa](https://pubs.aip.org/aip/jap/article/132/16/160902/2837574/The-"
"future-of-quantum-computing-with) berbanding komputer klasik yang digunakan "
"hari ini, keselamatan kriptografi perlu dinilai semula untuk dunia di mana "
"komputer kuantum mungkin <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Pertumbuhan, "
"peningkatan, atau pendaraban sesuatu perkara dengan pantas atau secara "
"eksponen, lazimnya dalam konteks biologi, teknologi, atau "
"abstrak.\">berkembang pesat</DefinitionTooltip>, membolehkan serangan "
"kriptografi baru yang tidak mungkin dilakukan menggunakan komputer klasik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These attacks may occur in future on data that is being transmitted or "
"stored now known as *harvest now, decrypt later*, so it is not sufficient to"
" wait until the required systems are available, but to make changes now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Serangan ini mungkin berlaku pada masa hadapan ke atas data yang sedang "
"dihantar atau disimpan sekarang, dikenali sebagai *tuai sekarang, "
"nyahsulitkan kemudian*, jadi tidak cukup untuk menunggu sehingga sistem yang"
" diperlukan tersedia, tetapi perlu membuat perubahan sekarang.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The field of <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Also known as Post Quantum or "
"Quantum-Resistant. Cryptographic algorithms, protocols, or systems that are "
"designed to withstand attacks from quantum computers. Even as quantum "
"computing technology progresses, the security of digital communication and "
"sensitive information needs to remains intact.\">**quantum-safe "
"cryptography**</DefinitionTooltip> (QSC) encompasses efforts to [identify "
"and develop cryptographic "
"schemes](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7) that can withstand "
"attacks both from quantum and classical computing systems. This is also "
"sometimes called **quantum-resistant**, or **post-quantum cryptography**.`\n"
msgstr ""
"Bidang <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Juga dikenali sebagai Pasca-Kuantum "
"atau Tahan-Kuantum. Algoritma kriptografi, protokol, atau sistem yang direka"
" bentuk untuk menahan serangan daripada komputer kuantum. Walaupun teknologi"
" pengkomputeran kuantum terus berkembang, keselamatan komunikasi digital dan"
" maklumat sensitif perlu kekal utuh.\">**kriptografi selamat-"
"kuantum**</DefinitionTooltip> (QSC) merangkumi usaha untuk [mengenal pasti "
"dan membangunkan skim "
"kriptografi](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7) yang dapat menahan "
"serangan daripada sistem pengkomputeran kuantum mahupun klasik. Ini "
"kadangkala juga disebut **tahan-kuantum**, atau **kriptografi pasca-"
"kuantum**.`\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In earlier lessons, we discussed some of the potential security risks that "
"the development of general-purpose quantum computers poses to a number of "
"traditional cryptographic primitives such as symmetric key algorithms, "
"cryptographic hash functions, and asymmetric key algorithms. Additionally, "
"we mentioned cryptographically relevant quantum algorithms and the protocols"
" they impact.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran-pelajaran terdahulu, kita telah membincangkan beberapa "
"risiko keselamatan berpotensi yang ditimbulkan oleh pembangunan komputer "
"kuantum tujuan umum terhadap beberapa primitif kriptografi tradisional "
"seperti algoritma kunci simetri, fungsi cincangan kriptografi, dan algoritma"
" kunci asimetri. Selain itu, kita telah menyebut tentang algoritma kuantum "
"yang berkaitan secara kriptografi dan protokol yang terjejas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that the most significant impacts of quantum algorithms occur in the "
"context of asymmetric key cryptography, where [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) offers a polynomial-"
"time solution to the prime factoring and <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Discrete Logarithm Problem. Finding the exponent to which a "
"given number (the base) must be raised to obtain another number (the "
"result), within a specified mathematical group. Solving this problem for "
"certain groups is computationally difficult, forming the basis for several "
"cryptographic schemes but Quantum Computers may have the potential to solve "
"this problem in the future.\">discrete logarithm</DefinitionTooltip> "
"problems. Therefore, asymmetric cryptosystems based on factoring and "
"discrete logarithms need to be replaced by new quantum-safe cryptography "
"schemes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita melihat bahawa impak paling ketara daripada algoritma kuantum berlaku "
"dalam konteks kriptografi kunci asimetri, di mana [algoritma "
"Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) menawarkan penyelesaian masa"
" polinomial kepada masalah pemfaktoran perdana dan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Masalah Logaritma Diskret. Mencari eksponen yang mana nombor "
"tertentu (asas) perlu dinaikkan kuasanya untuk mendapatkan nombor lain "
"(hasil), dalam kumpulan matematik yang ditetapkan. Menyelesaikan masalah ini"
" untuk kumpulan tertentu adalah sukar secara pengiraan, menjadi asas kepada "
"beberapa skim kriptografi tetapi Komputer Kuantum mungkin berpotensi "
"menyelesaikan masalah ini pada masa hadapan.\">logaritma "
"diskret</DefinitionTooltip>. Oleh itu, sistem kripto asimetri berasaskan "
"pemfaktoran dan logaritma diskret perlu digantikan dengan skim kriptografi "
"selamat-kuantum yang baru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is in contrast to the symmetric key and cryptographic hashing protocols"
" impacted by the Grover and [BHT](https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0054319) "
"algorithms, where the quantum speedups are not super-polynomial. Therefore, "
"in this latter case, existing algorithms such as AES and SHA-256 can be "
"fortified at least in the medium term by ensuring sufficiently long key and "
"hash lengths.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini berbeza dengan protokol kunci simetri dan pencincangan kriptografi yang "
"terjejas oleh algoritma Grover dan "
"[BHT](https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0054319), di mana peningkatan kelajuan "
"kuantum bukanlah superpolinomial. Oleh itu, dalam kes yang terakhir ini, "
"algoritma sedia ada seperti AES dan SHA-256 boleh diperkukuh sekurang-"
"kurangnya dalam jangka sederhana dengan memastikan panjang kunci dan "
"cincangan yang mencukupi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum algorithms and impacts to cryptography {#quantum-algorithms-and-"
"impacts-to-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum dan impak kepada kriptografi {#quantum-algorithms-and-"
"impacts-to-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Quantum Algorithm | Functionality      | <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"As defined by the [NIST](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/security_strength): *A number characterizing the amount of work that is expected to suffice to defeat an implemented cryptographic mechanism (for example, by compromising its functionality and/or circumventing the protection that its use was intended to facilitate). Security strength is often expressed in bits. If the security strength of a particular implementation of a cryptographic mechanism is s bits, it is expected that the equivalent of (roughly) 2<sup>s</sup> basic operations of some sort will be sufficient to defeat it in some way.*\">Security Strength</DefinitionTooltip> ($n$ = number of bits) | Impacted Cryptographic Protocols                 | Mitigation             |\n"
"|-------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n"
"| Shor              | factoring          | $poly(n)$                                            | RSA                                              | Migrate to QSC         |\n"
"| Shor              | discrete logarithm | $poly(n)$                                            | Diffie-Hellman, DSA, Elliptic Curve Cryptography | Migrate to QSC         |\n"
"| Grover            | key search         | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Symmetric key algorithms (for example, AES)             | Sufficient key length  |\n"
"| Grover            | pre-image attack   | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Hash functions (for example, SHA-256)                   | Sufficient hash length |\n"
"| BHT               | collision attack   | $2^{n/3}$ or $2^{2n/5}$                              | Hash functions (for example, SHA-256)                   | Sufficient hash length |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Algoritma Kuantum | Fungsi             | <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Sebagaimana yang ditakrifkan oleh [NIST](https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/security_strength): *Satu nombor yang menggambarkan jumlah kerja yang dijangka memadai untuk mengalahkan mekanisme kriptografi yang dilaksanakan (contohnya, dengan menjejaskan fungsinya dan/atau memintas perlindungan yang penggunaannya bertujuan untuk memudahkan). Kekuatan keselamatan sering dinyatakan dalam bit. Jika kekuatan keselamatan bagi pelaksanaan tertentu sesuatu mekanisme kriptografi ialah s bit, dijangkakan bahawa setara dengan (kira-kira) 2<sup>s</sup> operasi asas sesuatu jenis akan mencukupi untuk mengalahkannya dalam sesuatu cara.*\">Kekuatan Keselamatan</DefinitionTooltip> ($n$ = bilangan bit) | Protokol Kriptografi Terjejas                    | Mitigasi               |\n"
"|-------------------|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|------------------------|\n"
"| Shor              | pemfaktoran        | $poly(n)$                                            | RSA                                              | Migrasi ke QSC         |\n"
"| Shor              | logaritma diskret  | $poly(n)$                                            | Diffie-Hellman, DSA, Kriptografi Lengkung Eliptik | Migrasi ke QSC         |\n"
"| Grover            | carian kunci       | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Algoritma kunci simetri (contohnya, AES)         | Panjang kunci mencukupi |\n"
"| Grover            | serangan praimage  | $2^{n/2}$                                            | Fungsi cincangan (contohnya, SHA-256)            | Panjang cincangan mencukupi |\n"
"| BHT               | serangan perlanggaran | $2^{n/3}$ atau $2^{2n/5}$                         | Fungsi cincangan (contohnya, SHA-256)            | Panjang cincangan mencukupi |\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basic principles of quantum-safe cryptography {#basic-principles-of-quantum-"
"safe-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Prinsip asas kriptografi selamat-kuantum {#basic-principles-of-quantum-safe-"
"cryptography}"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Computational complexity {#computational-complexity}"
msgstr "Kerumitan pengiraan {#computational-complexity}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In cryptography, the *computational complexity class* [**NP (non-"
"deterministic polynomial "
"time)**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP_(complexity)&oldid=1158889203)"
" plays an important role. This class consists of decision problems for which"
" proposed solutions can be verified in polynomial time using a "
"<DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Machine that operates on an infinite tape "
"containing symbols which has a read/write head that can move left or right "
"on the tape and change the symbols according to a set of predetermined "
"rules. In a deterministic Turing machine, the transition from one state to "
"another is uniquely determined by the current state and the symbol being "
"read from the tape. This means that for any given configuration of the "
"machine, there is only one possible next step.\">deterministic Turing "
"machine</DefinitionTooltip> (DTM). The importance of NP stems from the fact "
"that it is conjectured to consist of many computational problems that cannot"
" be solved efficiently by both classical and quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kriptografi, *kelas kerumitan pengiraan* [**NP (masa polinomial bukan "
"deterministik)**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP_(complexity)&oldid=1158889203)"
" memainkan peranan penting. Kelas ini terdiri daripada masalah keputusan "
"yang penyelesaian yang dicadangkan boleh disahkan dalam masa polinomial "
"menggunakan <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Mesin yang beroperasi pada pita "
"tidak terhingga yang mengandungi simbol, yang mempunyai kepala baca/tulis "
"yang boleh bergerak ke kiri atau kanan pada pita dan menukar simbol mengikut"
" set peraturan yang telah ditetapkan. Dalam mesin Turing deterministik, "
"peralihan daripada satu keadaan ke keadaan lain ditentukan secara unik oleh "
"keadaan semasa dan simbol yang dibaca daripada pita. Ini bermakna untuk "
"sebarang konfigurasi mesin yang diberikan, hanya ada satu langkah seterusnya"
" yang mungkin.\">mesin Turing deterministik</DefinitionTooltip> (DTM). "
"Kepentingan NP berpunca daripada andaian bahawa ia terdiri daripada banyak "
"masalah pengiraan yang tidak boleh diselesaikan dengan cekap oleh komputer "
"klasik mahupun kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first generation of successful asymmetric key cryptosystems developed in"
" the 1970s based their security on mathematical problems such as prime "
"factorization and discrete logarithms that are now conjectured to belong to "
"the **NP-intermediate** subclass of NP. This subclass consists of problems "
"that are believed not to have polynomial-time solutions on DTMs but at the "
"same time are also not as hard as the hardest problems in NP.\n"
msgstr ""
"Generasi pertama sistem kripto kunci asimetri yang berjaya dibangunkan pada "
"tahun 1970-an mengasaskan keselamatannya pada masalah matematik seperti "
"pemfaktoran perdana dan logaritma diskret yang kini diandaikan tergolong "
"dalam subkelas **NP-pertengahan** NP. Subkelas ini terdiri daripada masalah "
"yang dipercayai tidak mempunyai penyelesaian masa polinomial pada DTM tetapi"
" pada masa yang sama juga tidak sesukar masalah-masalah paling sukar dalam "
"NP.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The latter belong to the subclass [**NP-"
"complete**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"completeness&oldid=1157123934). Following [Shor's "
"algorithm](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) in the 1990s, it became"
" clear that at least some NP-intermediate problems are amenable to efficient"
" solutions on quantum computers that are not DTMs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang terakhir itu tergolong dalam subkelas [**NP-"
"lengkap**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"completeness&oldid=1157123934). Berikutan [algoritma "
"Shor](https://doi.org/10.1109/SFCS.1994.365700) pada tahun 1990-an, menjadi "
"jelas bahawa sekurang-kurangnya sesetengah masalah NP-pertengahan mudah "
"diselesaikan dengan cekap pada komputer kuantum yang bukan DTM.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Therefore, modern quantum-safe cryptography schemes are based on NP-complete"
" problems or related [**NP-"
"hard**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"hardness&oldid=1153995836) problems, which currently are not known to be "
"solvable efficiently even on quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh itu, skim kriptografi selamat-kuantum moden berasaskan masalah NP-"
"lengkap atau masalah [**NP-"
"sukar**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NP-"
"hardness&oldid=1153995836) yang berkaitan, yang pada masa ini tidak "
"diketahui boleh diselesaikan dengan cekap walaupun pada komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Average vs worst-case hardness {#average-vs-worst-case-hardness}"
msgstr ""
"Kesukaran kes purata berbanding kes terburuk {#average-vs-worst-case-"
"hardness}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While there are many known NP-hard problems, not every such problem is "
"suitable as a basis for cryptographic security. In this context, the notion "
"of [**average-case "
"hardness**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Computational_hardness_assumption&oldid=1158033193)"
" is useful for cryptography. A problem is **average-case hard** if most "
"instances of the problem drawn randomly from some distribution are hard, "
"whereas a problem is **worst-case hard** if it is hard only on some isolated"
" *worst-case* instances. Quantum-safe cryptologists therefore search for "
"mathematical problems that satisfy the assumption of average-case hardness "
"and employ theoretical tools such as worst-case to average-case "
"[reductions](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) to identify suitable protocols"
" whose security and efficiency can be guaranteed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun terdapat banyak masalah NP-sukar yang diketahui, tidak setiap "
"masalah sedemikian sesuai sebagai asas untuk keselamatan kriptografi. Dalam "
"konteks ini, konsep [**kesukaran kes "
"purata**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Computational_hardness_assumption&oldid=1158033193)"
" berguna untuk kriptografi. Sesuatu masalah dikatakan **sukar kes purata** "
"jika kebanyakan contoh masalah yang diambil secara rawak dari sesetengah "
"taburan adalah sukar, manakala masalah dikatakan **sukar kes terburuk** jika"
" ia hanya sukar pada beberapa contoh *kes terburuk* yang terpencil. Oleh "
"itu, pakar kripto selamat-kuantum mencari masalah matematik yang memenuhi "
"andaian kesukaran kes purata dan menggunakan alat teori seperti pengurangan "
"kes terburuk ke kes purata untuk mengenal pasti protokol yang sesuai yang "
"keselamatan dan kecekapannya dapat dijamin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical structures {#mathematical-structures}"
msgstr "Struktur matematik {#mathematical-structures}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cryptologists have put forth a number of different mathematical structures "
"that satisfy the necessary hardness requirements as potential candidates for"
" quantum-safe migration of asymmetric key cryptosystems. Some well-known "
"families include:\n"
msgstr ""
"Para pakar kripto telah mengemukakan beberapa struktur matematik berbeza "
"yang memenuhi keperluan kesukaran yang diperlukan sebagai calon berpotensi "
"untuk migrasi selamat-kuantum bagi sistem kripto kunci asimetri. Beberapa "
"keluarga yang terkenal termasuk:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Lattice-based cryptography:**](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) This "
"class of algorithms relies on the hardness of problems such as the shortest "
"vector problem (SVP) and the closest vector problem (CVP) in [lattice "
"structures](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)."
" Notable lattice-based schemes include "
"[NTRU](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NTRU&oldid=1107481357) and"
" [Learning with Errors](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26) (LWE).\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berasaskan kekisi:**](http://arxiv.org/abs/2208.08125) Kelas "
"algoritma ini bergantung pada kesukaran masalah seperti masalah vektor "
"terpendek (SVP) dan masalah vektor terdekat (CVP) dalam [struktur "
"kekisi](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)."
" Skim berasaskan kekisi yang terkenal termasuk "
"[NTRU](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=NTRU&oldid=1107481357) dan"
" [Pembelajaran dengan Ralat](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26) (LWE).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Code-based cryptography:**](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7_4) "
"This type of cryptography is based on the difficulty of decoding a general "
"linear code. The most notable example is the [McEliece "
"cryptosystem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=McEliece_cryptosystem&oldid=1158412532).\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berasaskan "
"kod:**](https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-540-88702-7_4) Jenis kriptografi ini "
"berasaskan kesukaran penyahkodan kod linear umum. Contoh paling terkenal "
"ialah [sistem kripto "
"McEliece](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=McEliece_cryptosystem&oldid=1158412532).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Multivariate "
"cryptography:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Multivariate_cryptography&oldid=1117344303)"
" These systems involve equations of multiple variables over a finite field. "
"A well-known system in this category is the HFE (Hidden Field Equations) "
"scheme.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi "
"multivariat:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Multivariate_cryptography&oldid=1117344303)"
" Sistem ini melibatkan persamaan berbilang pemboleh ubah ke atas medan "
"terhingga. Sistem terkenal dalam kategori ini ialah skim HFE (Persamaan "
"Medan Tersembunyi).\n"

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Hash-based "
"cryptography:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hash-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1159153101) These are cryptographic systems that "
"use only cryptographic hash functions. They are often used for digital "
"signatures, like the Merkle signature scheme.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berasaskan "
"cincangan:**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Hash-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1159153101) Ini adalah sistem kriptografi yang "
"hanya menggunakan fungsi cincangan kriptografi. Sering digunakan untuk "
"tandatangan digital, seperti skim tandatangan Merkle.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '5. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[**Isogeny-based "
"cryptography:**](https://www.computer.org/csdl/magazine/it/2019/06/08896171/1eS9UwZEbjG)"
" These systems are based on the difficulty of certain problems in the "
"algebraic structure of elliptic curves. [Supersingular Isogeny Diffie-"
"Hellman](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Supersingular_isogeny_key_exchange&oldid=1163291033)"
" (SIDH) is an example.\n"
msgstr ""
"[**Kriptografi berasaskan "
"isogeni:**](https://www.computer.org/csdl/magazine/it/2019/06/08896171/1eS9UwZEbjG)"
" Sistem ini berasaskan kesukaran masalah tertentu dalam struktur algebra "
"lengkung eliptik. [Pertukaran Kunci Diffie-Hellman Isogeni "
"Supersingular](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Supersingular_isogeny_key_exchange&oldid=1163291033)"
" (SIDH) adalah contohnya.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"NIST standardization of quantum-safe cryptography {#nist-standardization-of-"
"quantum-safe-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Penstandardan NIST bagi kriptografi selamat-kuantum {#nist-standardization-"
"of-quantum-safe-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recognizing the potential impact of quantum computing on current "
"cryptographic systems, NIST initiated a program to standardize quantum-safe "
"cryptographic algorithms in 2016 using a process similar to the one NIST "
"followed to standardize the Advanced Encryption Standard (AES) in the early "
"2000s. In an open and transparent process involving security domain "
"stakeholders, several QSC candidates were submitted for evaluation, and "
"following a six-year review process, [NIST announced a list of four "
"finalists](https://www.nist.gov/news-events/news/2022/07/nist-announces-"
"first-four-quantum-resistant-cryptographic-algorithms) to become a part of "
"NIST’s quantum-safe cryptographic standard.\n"
msgstr ""
"Menyedari impak berpotensi pengkomputeran kuantum terhadap sistem "
"kriptografi semasa, NIST memulakan program untuk menstandardkan algoritma "
"kriptografi selamat-kuantum pada tahun 2016 menggunakan proses yang serupa "
"dengan yang diikuti NIST untuk menstandardkan Piawaian Penyulitan Lanjutan "
"(AES) pada awal tahun 2000-an. Dalam proses yang terbuka dan telus "
"melibatkan pemegang taruh domain keselamatan, beberapa calon QSC telah "
"dikemukakan untuk penilaian, dan setelah proses semakan selama enam tahun, "
"[NIST mengumumkan senarai empat finalis](https://www.nist.gov/news-"
"events/news/2022/07/nist-announces-first-four-quantum-resistant-"
"cryptographic-algorithms) untuk menjadi sebahagian daripada piawaian "
"kriptografi selamat-kuantum NIST.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finalists of the first NIST quantum-safe cryptography standardization effort"
" {#finalists-of-the-first-nist-quantum-safe-cryptography-standardization-"
"effort}"
msgstr ""
"Finalis usaha penstandardan kriptografi selamat-kuantum NIST yang pertama "
"{#finalists-of-the-first-nist-quantum-safe-cryptography-standardization-"
"effort}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| QSC Algorithm      | Cryptographic family | Application                     |\n"
"|--------------------|----------------------|---------------------------------|\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Kyber     | Lattice-based        | Key encapsulation mechanism     |\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Dilithium | Lattice-based        | Digital signatures              |\n"
"| FALCON             | Lattice-based        | Lightweight digital signatures |\n"
"| SPHINCS+           | Hash-based           | Digital Signatures              |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Algoritma QSC      | Keluarga kriptografi | Aplikasi                         |\n"
"|--------------------|----------------------|----------------------------------|\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Kyber     | Berasaskan kekisi    | Mekanisme enkapsulasi kunci      |\n"
"| CRYSTALS-Dilithium | Berasaskan kekisi    | Tandatangan digital              |\n"
"| FALCON             | Berasaskan kekisi    | Tandatangan digital ringan       |\n"
"| SPHINCS+           | Berasaskan cincangan | Tandatangan Digital              |\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of the four NIST finalists, three are lattice-based and one, "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/), is hash-based. The Kyber and Dilithium "
"algorithms, part of the [CRYSTALS cryptographic suite](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/), were selected to be general-purpose protocols for key "
"encapsulation and digital signatures, respectively. "
"[FALCON](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Falcon_(signature_scheme)&oldid=1157852190)"
" was recommended for applications requiring smaller digital signatures than "
"those provided by Dilithium. [SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/) meanwhile was "
"primarily chosen as a backup option to the lattice-based approaches, as it "
"uses a different mathematical structure. Lattice-based cryptography "
"therefore seems well-positioned to form the basis for the first-generation "
"of QSC standards.\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada empat finalis NIST, tiga berasaskan kekisi dan satu, "
"[SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/), berasaskan cincangan. Algoritma Kyber dan "
"Dilithium, yang merupakan sebahagian daripada [suite kriptografi "
"CRYSTALS](https://pq-crystals.org/), dipilih sebagai protokol tujuan umum "
"untuk enkapsulasi kunci dan tandatangan digital masing-masing. "
"[FALCON](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Falcon_(signature_scheme)&oldid=1157852190)"
" disyorkan untuk aplikasi yang memerlukan tandatangan digital lebih kecil "
"daripada yang disediakan oleh Dilithium. [SPHINCS+](https://sphincs.org/) "
"pula dipilih terutamanya sebagai pilihan sandaran kepada pendekatan "
"berasaskan kekisi, kerana ia menggunakan struktur matematik yang berbeza. "
"Kriptografi berasaskan kekisi oleh itu kelihatan berada dalam kedudukan baik"
" untuk membentuk asas bagi standard QSC generasi pertama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In August 2023, [NIST published three draft standards](https://csrc.nist.gov/news/2023/three-draft-fips-for-post-quantum-cryptography) for comments - which include the algorithms above:\n"
"- [FIPS 203, Module-Lattice-Based Key-Encapsulation Mechanism Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 204, Module-Lattice-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 205, Stateless Hash-Based Digital Signature Standard](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/ipd)\n"
msgstr ""
"Pada Ogos 2023, [NIST menerbitkan tiga draf piawaian](https://csrc.nist.gov/news/2023/three-draft-fips-for-post-quantum-cryptography) untuk ulasan - yang merangkumi algoritma di atas:\n"
"- [FIPS 203, Piawaian Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci Berasaskan Kekisi-Modul](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 204, Piawaian Tandatangan Digital Berasaskan Kekisi-Modul](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/204/ipd)\n"
"- [FIPS 205, Piawaian Tandatangan Digital Berasaskan Cincangan Tanpa Keadaan](https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/205/ipd)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lattice-based cryptography {#lattice-based-cryptography}"
msgstr "Kriptografi berasaskan kekisi {#lattice-based-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As the name suggests, [lattice-based "
"cryptography](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1163912863) (LBC) is based on the hardness of "
"certain problems defined on mathematical structures called "
"[**lattices**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985).\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti namanya, [kriptografi berasaskan "
"kekisi](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice-"
"based_cryptography&oldid=1163912863) (LBC) berasaskan kesukaran masalah-"
"masalah tertentu yang ditakrifkan pada struktur matematik yang dipanggil "
"[**kekisi**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Of fundamental importance are two computational problems on lattices, namely"
" the **shortest vector problem** and the **learning with errors problem**, "
"which we discuss below after some preliminary definitions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua masalah pengiraan pada kekisi yang paling asas ialah **masalah vektor "
"terpendek** dan **masalah pembelajaran dengan ralat**, yang kita bincangkan "
"di bawah setelah beberapa takrifan awal.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Lattices {#lattices}"
msgstr "Kekisi {#lattices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think of what a lattice is in the world around us. The Eiffel tower "
"(Paris), or Birds-nest stadium (Beijing). Those structures have many linked "
"elements which can be thought of as a series of points joined together along"
" straight lines.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh memikirkan apakah kekisi itu dalam dunia di sekeliling kita. "
"Menara Eiffel (Paris), atau stadium Sarang Burung (Beijing). Struktur-"
"struktur tersebut mempunyai banyak elemen yang berhubung, yang boleh "
"dianggap sebagai satu siri titik yang disambungkan sepanjang garis lurus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Diamonds are another form of lattice. There is a clear, repeating structure "
"of Carbon atoms. They are then effectively joined together by atomic bonds; "
"and this structure that is formed is what gives diamond its unique "
"properties. However, different crystal structures can have very different "
"layouts (can be thought of as our lattice structure), and therefore ends up "
"with distinct features. Hence, lattices serve as the foundational "
"mathematical framework that dictates the unique traits of different "
"structures which we use in cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Berlian adalah satu lagi bentuk kekisi. Terdapat struktur yang jelas dan "
"berulang daripada atom Karbon. Atom-atom itu kemudiannya secara efektif "
"disambungkan oleh ikatan atom; dan struktur yang terbentuk inilah yang "
"memberikan berlian sifat-sifat uniknya. Walau bagaimanapun, struktur kristal"
" yang berbeza boleh mempunyai susun atur yang sangat berbeza (boleh dianggap"
" sebagai struktur kekisi kita), dan oleh itu akhirnya mempunyai ciri-ciri "
"yang tersendiri. Oleh itu, kekisi berfungsi sebagai kerangka matematik asas "
"yang menentukan sifat unik struktur-struktur berbeza yang kita gunakan dalam"
" kriptografi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In simple mathematical terms, a lattice can be thought of as a collection of"
" regularly spaced points that repeat at fixed intervals. To describe how "
"these points are positioned relative to each other, we use vectors. The "
"specific arrangement of these vectors, which defines the layout of the "
"lattice, is referred to as the *basis.*\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam istilah matematik yang mudah, kekisi boleh dianggap sebagai koleksi "
"titik-titik yang tersusun sekata yang berulang pada selang tetap. Untuk "
"menerangkan bagaimana titik-titik ini diletakkan berbanding antara satu sama"
" lain, kita menggunakan vektor. Susunan khusus vektor-vektor ini, yang "
"menentukan tataletak kekisi, dirujuk sebagai *asas.*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Imagine you have a box of toy construction bricks, and you want to build "
"various objects with the same set of pieces. Each unique object you create "
"requires a specific arrangement, and the way you choose and arrange the "
"bricks serves as the *basis* for constructing different objects. If you "
"change the selection or arrangement of bricks, you get a different object "
"with distinct characteristics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bayangkan anda mempunyai kotak bata permainan binaan, dan anda ingin membina"
" pelbagai objek dengan set kepingan yang sama. Setiap objek unik yang anda "
"cipta memerlukan susunan tertentu, dan cara anda memilih dan menyusun bata "
"berfungsi sebagai *asas* untuk membina objek-objek berbeza. Jika anda "
"menukar pilihan atau susunan bata, anda mendapat objek berbeza dengan ciri-"
"ciri yang tersendiri.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, in a lattice, the *basis* is like the set of atomic building "
"blocks that define the lattice's structure. Depending on how you arrange "
"these building blocks (atoms or points) in the lattice, you can create "
"various lattice structures with different properties. Just as changing the "
"toy construction brick pieces changes the object you build, altering the "
"basis changes the lattice's characteristics and properties.\n"
msgstr ""
"Begitu juga, dalam kekisi, *asas* adalah seperti set blok binaan atom yang "
"menentukan struktur kekisi. Bergantung pada cara anda menyusun blok binaan "
"ini (atom atau titik) dalam kekisi, anda boleh mencipta pelbagai struktur "
"kekisi dengan sifat berbeza. Sama seperti menukar kepingan bata permainan "
"binaan mengubah objek yang dibina, mengubah asas mengubah ciri-ciri dan "
"sifat kekisi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It's important to note that lattices are not limited to two or three "
"dimensions; they can extend to higher dimensions, and in fields like "
"cryptography, they may involve 1000s or more dimensions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penting untuk diperhatikan bahawa kekisi tidak terhad kepada dua atau tiga "
"dimensi; ia boleh meluas ke dimensi yang lebih tinggi, dan dalam bidang "
"seperti kriptografi, ia mungkin melibatkan ribuan atau lebih dimensi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of lattices\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penerangan matematik kekisi\">\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given $n$ linearly independent vectors $A = "
"\\{\\mathbf{v_1},...,\\mathbf{v_n} | \\mathbf{v_i} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m\\}$, "
"the *lattice* $\\mathcal{L}$ generated by $A$ is the set of integer linear "
"combinations $\\mathcal{L} = \\{ \\sum_i c_i \\mathbf{v_i} | c_i \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z} \\}$\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan $n$ vektor bebas linear $A = \\{\\mathbf{v_1},...,\\mathbf{v_n} | "
"\\mathbf{v_i} \\in \\mathbb{R}^m\\}$, *kekisi* $\\mathcal{L}$ yang dijana "
"oleh $A$ ialah set kombinasi linear integer $\\mathcal{L} = \\{ \\sum_i c_i "
"\\mathbf{v_i} | c_i \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\}$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A *basis* $B$ of a lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ is any set of linearly independent"
" vectors $B=\\{b_1,...,b_n\\}$  that spans the lattice i.e, $\\mathcal{L}(B)"
" = \\{ \\sum_i z_i b_i | z_i \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Asas* $B$ bagi kekisi $\\mathcal{L}$ ialah sebarang set vektor bebas linear"
" $B=\\{b_1,...,b_n\\}$ yang merentangi kekisi iaitu, $\\mathcal{L}(B) = \\{ "
"\\sum_i z_i b_i | z_i \\in \\mathbb{Z} \\}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Importantly, the basis for a given lattice is not unique. Two different "
"basis sets $B, B^{\\prime}$ can describe the same lattice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Yang penting, asas bagi kekisi tertentu tidak unik. Dua set asas yang "
"berbeza $B, B^{\\prime}$ boleh menerangkan kekisi yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Not every basis is unique - it may just be a different perspective of the "
"same structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tidak setiap asas adalah unik - ia mungkin hanya perspektif berbeza bagi "
"struktur yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This leads to an important concept in lattice mathematics, that of "
"[*lattice-basis "
"reduction*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_reduction&oldid=1139588628)."
" This is the process of taking a given integer lattice and attempting to "
"find a *good* basis comprising short, nearly orthogonal vectors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini membawa kepada konsep penting dalam matematik kekisi, iaitu "
"[*pengurangan asas "
"kekisi*](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_reduction&oldid=1139588628)."
" Ini adalah proses mengambil kekisi integer yang diberikan dan cuba mencari "
"asas yang *baik* yang terdiri daripada vektor pendek yang hampir ortogon.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 1: Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis v_1,"
" v_2 to a good basis u_1, u_2](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/Lattice-reduction-wiki.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 1: Pengurangan asas kekisi dalam dua dimensi daripada asas \"buruk\" "
"v_1, v_2 kepada asas baik u_1, u_2](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/Lattice-reduction-wiki.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 1. Lattice-basis reduction in two dimensions from a \"bad\" basis "
"$v_1$, $v_2$ to a good basis $u_1$, $u_2$*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rajah 1. Pengurangan asas kekisi dalam dua dimensi daripada asas \"buruk\" "
"$v_1$, $v_2$ kepada asas baik $u_1$, $u_2$*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Lattice-basis reductions can be performed in polynomial-time using the "
"[**Lenstra–Lenstra–Lovász** "
"algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lenstra%E2%80%93Lenstra%E2%80%93Lov%C3%A1sz_lattice_basis_reduction_algorithm&oldid=1151925724)"
" (LLL).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pengurangan asas kekisi boleh dilakukan dalam masa polinomial menggunakan "
"[algoritma "
"**Lenstra–Lenstra–Lovász**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lenstra%E2%80%93Lenstra%E2%80%93Lov%C3%A1sz_lattice_basis_reduction_algorithm&oldid=1151925724)"
" (LLL).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The shortest vector problem {#the-shortest-vector-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah vektor terpendek {#the-shortest-vector-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **shortest vector problem** (SVP) is the challenge of finding the "
"shortest distance (vector), between any two points in the lattice\n"
msgstr ""
"**Masalah vektor terpendek** (SVP) adalah cabaran mencari jarak (vektor) "
"terpendek antara mana-mana dua titik dalam kekisi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of the SVP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penerangan matematik SVP\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given a lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ embedded in a vector space $\\mathcal{V}$ "
"with norm $N$, the "
"[SVP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)"
" asks for the shortest non-zero vector in $\\mathcal{L}$ as measured by $N$,"
" that is, find a vector $v$ such that its length $\\|v\\|_N = "
"\\min\\limits_{v^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L} \\smallsetminus "
"\\{\\mathbf{0}\\}} \\|v^{\\prime}\\|_N = \\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan kekisi $\\mathcal{L}$ yang tertanam dalam ruang vektor "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ dengan norma $N$, "
"[SVP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Lattice_problem&oldid=1149662985)"
" meminta vektor bukan sifar terpendek dalam $\\mathcal{L}$ sebagaimana yang "
"diukur oleh $N$, iaitu, cari vektor $v$ supaya panjangnya $\\|v\\|_N = "
"\\min\\limits_{v^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L} \\smallsetminus "
"\\{\\mathbf{0}\\}} \\|v^{\\prime}\\|_N = \\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 2: The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The "
"orange vector is the shortest vector](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/SVP.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 2: SVP pada kekisi yang ditentukan oleh vektor asas b_1, b_2: Vektor "
"oren ialah vektor terpendek](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/SVP.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 2. The SVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors $b_1$, $b_2$: The"
" yellow vector is the shortest vector*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rajah 2. SVP pada kekisi yang ditentukan oleh vektor asas $b_1$, $b_2$: "
"Vektor kuning ialah vektor terpendek*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Miklós Ajtai has shown that the shortest vector problem is **NP-"
"hard**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237838) in the worst case for "
"certain random lattices, even when lattice-basis reduction to a *good* basis"
" is possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Miklós Ajtai telah menunjukkan bahawa masalah vektor terpendek adalah **NP-"
"sukar**](https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/237814.237838) dalam kes terburuk "
"untuk kekisi rawak tertentu, walaupun apabila pengurangan asas kekisi kepada"
" asas yang *baik* adalah mungkin.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ajtai also demonstrated that there exists a worst-case to average-case "
"reduction for the shortest vector problem, laying the foundation for its use"
" in cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ajtai juga menunjukkan bahawa terdapat pengurangan kes terburuk ke kes "
"purata untuk masalah vektor terpendek, meletakkan asas bagi penggunaannya "
"dalam kriptografi.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The closest vector problem {#the-closest-vector-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah vektor terdekat {#the-closest-vector-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the **closest vector problem** (CVP) we are looking to find the closest "
"point on the lattice to the origin, or location given.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam **masalah vektor terdekat** (CVP) kita ingin mencari titik terdekat "
"pada kekisi kepada titik asal, atau lokasi yang diberikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The CVP is also known to be NP-hard.\n"
msgstr "CVP juga diketahui sebagai NP-sukar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Fig 3: The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors b_1, b_2: The red "
"point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external vector "
"shown in green that is not on the lattice](/learning/images/courses/quantum-"
"safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-cryptography/CVP.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Fig 3: CVP pada kekisi yang ditentukan oleh vektor asas b_1, b_2: Titik "
"merah mewakili vektor kekisi terdekat kepada vektor luaran yang diberikan "
"ditunjukkan dalam hijau yang tidak berada pada "
"kekisi](/learning/images/courses/quantum-safe-cryptography/quantum-safe-"
"cryptography/CVP.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Figure 3. The CVP on a lattice specified by basis vectors $b_1$, $b_2$: The"
" red point represents the closest lattice vector to the given external "
"vector shown in green that is not on the lattice*\n"
msgstr ""
"*Rajah 3. CVP pada kekisi yang ditentukan oleh vektor asas $b_1$, $b_2$: "
"Titik merah mewakili vektor kekisi terdekat kepada vektor luaran yang "
"diberikan ditunjukkan dalam hijau yang tidak berada pada kekisi*\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The *shortest vector problem* is a special case of the *closest vector "
"problem*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Masalah vektor terpendek* adalah kes khas bagi *masalah vektor terdekat*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of CVP\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penerangan matematik CVP\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A lattice $\\mathcal{L}$ embedded in a vector space $\\mathcal{V}$ with "
"metric $M$ is given, along with a vector $v$ in $\\mathcal{V}$ but not "
"necessarily in $\\mathcal{L}$. The task then is to find the vector $u$ in "
"$\\mathcal{L}$ closest to $v$ as measured by $M$ that is, $d_M (u, v) = "
"\\min\\limits_{u^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L}} d_M(u^{\\prime}, v)$ where "
"$d_M$ is the distance function of the metric $M$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Diberikan kekisi $\\mathcal{L}$ yang tertanam dalam ruang vektor "
"$\\mathcal{V}$ dengan metrik $M$, bersama vektor $v$ dalam $\\mathcal{V}$ "
"tetapi tidak semestinya dalam $\\mathcal{L}$. Tugas kemudiannya adalah "
"mencari vektor $u$ dalam $\\mathcal{L}$ yang paling dekat kepada $v$ "
"sebagaimana yang diukur oleh $M$ iaitu, $d_M (u, v) = "
"\\min\\limits_{u^{\\prime} \\in \\mathcal{L}} d_M(u^{\\prime}, v)$ di mana "
"$d_M$ ialah fungsi jarak bagi metrik $M$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The bounded distance decoding problem {#the-bounded-distance-decoding-"
"problem}"
msgstr ""
"Masalah penyahkodan jarak terbatas {#the-bounded-distance-decoding-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Very similar to the CVP is the [**bounded distance "
"decoding**](https://doi.org/10.1007/11830924_41) (BDD) problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sangat mirip dengan CVP ialah masalah [**penyahkodan jarak "
"terbatas**](https://doi.org/10.1007/11830924_41) (BDD).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this case we know that the origin supplied is close to the lattice, but "
"not *how close*, ie *bounded*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kes ini kita tahu bahawa titik asal yang diberikan adalah dekat dengan"
" kekisi, tetapi tidak *seberapa dekat*, iaitu *terbatas*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematical description of the BDD problem\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Penerangan matematik masalah BDD\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is additionally specified that the external vector $v$ is at most within "
"a distance $\\sigma\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$, where $\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$ "
"is the length of the shortest vector in the lattice and $\\sigma$ is a small"
" parameter.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ia ditentukan tambahan bahawa vektor luaran $v$ berada pada jarak paling "
"jauh $\\sigma\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$, di mana $\\lambda(\\mathcal{L})$ ialah"
" panjang vektor terpendek dalam kekisi dan $\\sigma$ ialah parameter "
"kecil.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The learning with errors problem {#the-learning-with-errors-problem}"
msgstr "Masalah pembelajaran dengan ralat {#the-learning-with-errors-problem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learning with errors (LWE) problem is based on the mathematics of "
"lattices combined with the idea of introducing errors into an equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah pembelajaran dengan ralat (LWE) berasaskan matematik kekisi yang "
"digabungkan dengan idea memasukkan ralat ke dalam persamaan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As is the case with any mathematical basis for cryptographic algorithms we "
"can easily introduce noise as we make a series of calculations, but trying "
"to find the inverse is very difficult.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti halnya dengan sebarang asas matematik untuk algoritma kriptografi, "
"kita boleh dengan mudah memasukkan hingar semasa membuat siri pengiraan, "
"tetapi cuba mencari songsangannya adalah sangat sukar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics of the LWE problem\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematik masalah LWE\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [learning with errors "
"problem](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Learning_with_errors&amp;oldid=1153719613)"
" ${\\mathrm{LWE}_{q,\\chi}}$ with modulus $q$ and error distribution $\\chi$"
" is: Given access only to polynomially many samples $(\\mathbf {a} ,t)$ of "
"choice from Alice's distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$, \"learn\" and "
"output the secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"[Masalah pembelajaran dengan "
"ralat](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Learning_with_errors&amp;oldid=1153719613)"
" ${\\mathrm{LWE}_{q,\\chi}}$ dengan modulus $q$ dan taburan ralat $\\chi$ "
"adalah: Diberikan akses hanya kepada sampel polinomial $(\\mathbf {a} ,t)$ "
"daripada taburan Alice $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$, \"pelajari\" dan keluarkan "
"vektor rahsia ${\\mathbf{s}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Let ${\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ be the ring of integers modulo $q$.\n"
msgstr "Biarkan ${\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ menjadi gelanggang integer modulo $q$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let ${\\mathbb {Z}_{q}^{n}}$ be the set of $n$-dimensional vectors over "
"${\\displaystyle \\mathbb{Z}_{q}}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Biarkan ${\\mathbb {Z}_{q}^{n}}$ menjadi set vektor $n$-dimensi ke atas "
"${\\displaystyle \\mathbb{Z}_{q}}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An adversary — say, Alice — chooses a fixed vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$ and keeps it a secret.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pihak lawan — katakan, Alice — memilih vektor tetap ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$ dan menyembunyikannya sebagai rahsia.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice also specifies $\\chi$, a fixed \"error\" probability distribution "
"over $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice juga menentukan $\\chi$, taburan kebarangkalian \"ralat\" tetap ke "
"atas $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Using the above ingredients, she constructs a distribution "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ on ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}\\times{\\mathbb {Z} "
"_{q}}$ as follows:\n"
msgstr ""
"Menggunakan bahan-bahan di atas, dia membina taburan $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi "
"}$ pada ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}\\times{\\mathbb {Z} _{q}}$ seperti berikut:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the uniform distribution over ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$, Alice chooses a "
"vector ${\\mathbf{a}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ .\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada taburan seragam ke atas ${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$, Alice memilih "
"vektor ${\\mathbf{a}}\\in {\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"From the given distribution $\\chi$, she picks a number $ {\\displaystyle "
"\\varepsilon \\in \\mathbb {Z} _{q} }$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Daripada taburan $\\chi$ yang diberikan, dia memilih nombor $ "
"{\\displaystyle \\varepsilon \\in \\mathbb {Z} _{q} }$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"She then evaluates ${\\displaystyle t=\\langle \\mathbf{a} ,\\mathbf {s} "
"\\rangle + \\varepsilon}$, where $\\langle\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{s}\\rangle "
"=\\sum_i a_{i}s_{i}$ is the standard inner product on "
"${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ and the addition is in $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dia kemudian menilai ${\\displaystyle t=\\langle \\mathbf{a} ,\\mathbf {s} "
"\\rangle + \\varepsilon}$, di mana $\\langle\\mathbf{a},\\mathbf{s}\\rangle "
"=\\sum_i a_{i}s_{i}$ ialah hasil darab dalam piawai pada "
"${\\mathbb{Z}}_{q}^{n}$ dan penambahan adalah dalam $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '    4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice outputs ${\\displaystyle (\\mathbf {a} ,t)}$.\n"
msgstr "Alice mengeluarkan ${\\displaystyle (\\mathbf {a} ,t)}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "    Note the errors introduced: $\\varepsilon$ drawn from $\\chi$\n"
msgstr ""
"    Perhatikan ralat yang dimasukkan: $\\varepsilon$ diambil daripada "
"$\\chi$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"    Early developments in the LWE problem employed the one-dimensional "
"discrete Gaussian distribution on $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$ as the error "
"distribution.\n"
msgstr ""
"    Perkembangan awal dalam masalah LWE menggunakan taburan Gaussian diskret"
" satu dimensi pada $\\mathbb {Z} _{q}$ sebagai taburan ralat.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The remarkable feature of the LWE problem is that without the errors, it "
"reduces to a set of linear equations that can be easily solved using a "
"technique like Gaussian elimination.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ciri luar biasa masalah LWE ialah tanpa ralat, ia turun kepada set persamaan"
" linear yang boleh diselesaikan dengan mudah menggunakan teknik seperti "
"penghapusan Gaussian.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"However, the inclusion of a suitable error distribution renders it an NP-"
"hard problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Walau bagaimanapun, kemasukan taburan ralat yang sesuai menjadikannya "
"masalah NP-sukar.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Encryption using the Learning with Errors cryptosystem {#encryption-using-"
"the-learning-with-errors-cryptosystem}"
msgstr ""
"Penyulitan menggunakan sistem kripto Pembelajaran dengan Ralat {#encryption-"
"using-the-learning-with-errors-cryptosystem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LWE problem discussed above leads to a public key cryptosystem "
"introduced by [Regev](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26).\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah LWE yang dibincangkan di atas membawa kepada sistem kripto kunci "
"awam yang diperkenalkan oleh [Regev](https://doi.org/10.1109/CCC.2010.26).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The exact process will be covered in the Python example below.\n"
msgstr "Proses tepat akan diliputi dalam contoh Python di bawah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics of key generation, encryption, and decryption\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematik penjanaan kunci, penyulitan, dan penyahsulitan\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Parameters:** The cryptosystem is characterized by the vector dimension or"
" security parameter $n$, modulus $q$, number of LWE samples $N$, and error "
"distribution $\\chi$. Typical choices that guarantee both security and "
"correctness are:\n"
msgstr ""
"**Parameter:** Sistem kripto dicirikan oleh dimensi vektor atau parameter "
"keselamatan $n$, modulus $q$, bilangan sampel LWE $N$, dan taburan ralat "
"$\\chi$. Pilihan tipikal yang menjamin keselamatan dan ketepatan ialah:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$q$ is a prime between $n^2$ and $2n^2$\n"
msgstr "$q$ ialah nombor perdana antara $n^2$ dan $2n^2$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$N = 1.1\\cdot~n~log~q$\n"
msgstr "$N = 1.1\\cdot~n~log~q$\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\chi = \\Psi_{\\alpha}$, with $\\alpha = 1/(\\sqrt{n}~log^2{n})$, where "
"$\\Psi_{\\alpha}$ is obtained by sampling the normal distribution "
"$\\mathcal{N}(0, \\alpha^2/(2\\pi))$ and reducing the result modulo 1\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\chi = \\Psi_{\\alpha}$, dengan $\\alpha = 1/(\\sqrt{n}~log^2{n})$, di "
"mana $\\Psi_{\\alpha}$ diperoleh dengan mensampling taburan normal "
"$\\mathcal{N}(0, \\alpha^2/(2\\pi))$ dan mengurangkan hasilnya modulo 1\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Private key:** The private key is the secret vector ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kunci peribadi:** Kunci peribadi ialah vektor rahsia ${\\mathbf{s}} \\in "
"{\\mathbb  {Z}}_{q}^{n}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Public key:** Choose $N$ samples $(\\mathbf{a}_i ,b_i)_{i=1}^N$ from the "
"LWE distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$\n"
msgstr ""
"**Kunci awam:** Pilih $N$ sampel $(\\mathbf{a}_i ,b_i)_{i=1}^N$ daripada "
"taburan LWE $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Encryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Penyulitan:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Encryption utilizes the public key and is carried out bit by bit.\n"
msgstr "Penyulitan menggunakan kunci awam dan dilakukan bit demi bit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For each bit of the message, randomly choose a binary vector $\\mathbf{r} "
"\\in \\{0,1\\}^N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk setiap bit mesej, pilih secara rawak vektor binari $\\mathbf{r} \\in "
"\\{0,1\\}^N$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the message bit is 0, the encryption is $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika bit mesej ialah 0, penyulitannya ialah $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the message bit is 1, the encryption is $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\lfloor \\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor + \\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika bit mesej ialah 1, penyulitannya ialah $(\\sum_i \\mathbf{a}_i r_i, "
"\\lfloor \\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor + \\sum_i b_i r_i)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**Decryption:**\n"
msgstr "**Penyahsulitan:**\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The decryption utilizes the private key ${\\mathbf{s}}$.\n"
msgstr "Penyahsulitan menggunakan kunci peribadi ${\\mathbf{s}}$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pair $({\\mathbf{a}, b })$ decrypts to $0$ if $b-\\langle "
"\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\mathbf{s}\\rangle$ is closer to $0$ than "
"$\\lfloor\\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor$ modulo $q$, else it decrypts to 1.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pasangan $({\\mathbf{a}, b })$ dinyahsulitkan kepada $0$ jika $b-\\langle "
"\\mathbf{a}\\cdot\\mathbf{s}\\rangle$ lebih dekat kepada $0$ daripada "
"$\\lfloor\\frac{q}{2}\\rfloor$ modulo $q$, jika tidak ia dinyahsulitkan "
"kepada 1.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The security of the LWE public key cryptosystem was analyzed by Regev:\n"
msgstr "Keselamatan sistem kripto kunci awam LWE telah dianalisis oleh Regev:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Firstly, it was shown that recovering the error/noise vector $\\mathbf{e} = "
"[\\varepsilon_1,...,\\varepsilon_N] \\leftarrow \\chi^N$ involved in the "
"construction of the public key is as hard as the bounded distance decoding "
"(BDD) problem, which, as noted above, is believed to be NP-hard. This "
"establishes the correspondence between LWE and explicit lattice problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, ditunjukkan bahawa mendapatkan semula vektor ralat/hingar "
"$\\mathbf{e} = [\\varepsilon_1,...,\\varepsilon_N] \\leftarrow \\chi^N$ yang"
" terlibat dalam pembinaan kunci awam adalah sesukar masalah penyahkodan "
"jarak terbatas (BDD), yang seperti yang dinyatakan di atas, dipercayai NP-"
"sukar. Ini mewujudkan hubungan antara LWE dan masalah kekisi yang "
"eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Secondly, security against chosen plain text attacks (CPA) is based on the "
"observation that an algorithm for distinguishing between encryptions of 0 "
"and 1 in the above cryptosystem can also distinguish between the "
"distribution $A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ and the uniform distribution over "
"$\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n} \\times \\mathbb{Z}_{q}$, which would imply a solution "
"of LWE itself.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua, keselamatan terhadap serangan teks biasa terpilih (CPA) berasaskan "
"pemerhatian bahawa algoritma untuk membezakan antara penyulitan 0 dan 1 "
"dalam sistem kripto di atas juga boleh membezakan antara taburan "
"$A_{\\mathbf{s},\\chi }$ dan taburan seragam ke atas $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n} "
"\\times \\mathbb{Z}_{q}$, yang akan membayangkan penyelesaian LWE itu "
"sendiri.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Illustration of LWE encryption in Python {#illustration-of-lwe-encryption-"
"in-python}"
msgstr ""
"Ilustrasi penyulitan LWE dalam Python {#illustration-of-lwe-encryption-in-"
"python}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following simple example shows the use of <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Learning With Errors. A mathematical technique which hides "
"secret information by introducing errors into equations, making them harder "
"to solve.\">LWE</DefinitionTooltip> for encryption and decryption. Bob will "
"send an encrypted message to Alice.\n"
msgstr ""
"Contoh mudah berikut menunjukkan penggunaan <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Pembelajaran Dengan Ralat. Teknik matematik yang menyembunyikan"
" maklumat rahsia dengan memasukkan ralat ke dalam persamaan, menjadikannya "
"lebih sukar untuk diselesaikan.\">LWE</DefinitionTooltip> untuk penyulitan "
"dan penyahsulitan. Bob akan menghantar mesej yang disulitkan kepada Alice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First, Alice and Bob agree on the **problem parameters**. These are "
"explained in detail in the maths section above, but in summary we require "
"$n, q, N, \\chi$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertama, Alice dan Bob bersetuju tentang **parameter masalah**. Ini "
"diterangkan secara terperinci dalam bahagian matematik di atas, tetapi "
"ringkasnya kita memerlukan $n, q, N, \\chi$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We start with some of the basic parameters\n"
msgstr "Kita mulakan dengan beberapa parameter asas\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$N$ represents the number of samples\n"
msgstr "$N$ mewakili bilangan sampel\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$q$ is a modulus\n"
msgstr "$q$ ialah modulus\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "n is known as the security parameter, or vector dimension.\n"
msgstr "n dikenali sebagai parameter keselamatan, atau dimensi vektor.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "These parameters are all public information in principle.\n"
msgstr "Parameter-parameter ini semuanya adalah maklumat awam pada dasarnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We also need a way of introducing errors\n"
msgstr "Kita juga memerlukan cara untuk memasukkan ralat\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here $\\chi$ represent the errors we want to introduce - we use a discrete "
"Gaussian distribution on $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}$ characterized by mean 0 and "
"standard deviation $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini $\\chi$ mewakili ralat yang ingin kita masukkan - kita menggunakan "
"taburan Gaussian diskret pada $\\mathbb{Z}_{q}$ yang dicirikan oleh min 0 "
"dan sisihan piawai $\\sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This definition of the errors to introduce is also public.\n"
msgstr "Definisi ralat yang hendak dimasukkan ini juga adalah awam.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So in Python, we need a simple function that approximates random error/noise"
" contributions $\\varepsilon$ drawn from a discrete Gaussian distribution "
"$\\chi$ with standard deviation $\\sigma$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jadi dalam Python, kita memerlukan fungsi mudah yang menganggarkan sumbangan"
" ralat/hingar rawak $\\varepsilon$ yang diambil daripada taburan Gaussian "
"diskret $\\chi$ dengan sisihan piawai $\\sigma$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some example values are printed so that you can see the distribution around "
"0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Beberapa nilai contoh dicetak supaya anda boleh melihat taburan sekitar 0.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next, Alice needs to generate her key pair.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, Alice perlu menjana pasangan kuncinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"She sets up her **private key** by choosing $n$ values between 0 and $q$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dia menetapkan **kunci peribadinya** dengan memilih $n$ nilai antara 0 dan "
"$q$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice now sets up her **public key**, by choosing random vectors, which are "
"then combined with the generated errors.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice kini menetapkan **kunci awamnya**, dengan memilih vektor rawak, yang "
"kemudian digabungkan dengan ralat yang dijana.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Mathematics\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Matematik\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "More precisely, she needs to generate the sample $A_{s,\\chi}$.\n"
msgstr "Lebih tepat lagi, dia perlu menjana sampel $A_{s,\\chi}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Accordingly, she randomly chooses vectors $\\mathbf{a} \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n}$ and errors $\\varepsilon$ from $\\chi$ to construct $N$"
" samples $(\\mathbf{a}, b)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sewajarnya, dia memilih secara rawak vektor $\\mathbf{a} \\in "
"\\mathbb{Z}_{q}^{n}$ dan ralat $\\varepsilon$ daripada $\\chi$ untuk membina"
" $N$ sampel $(\\mathbf{a}, b)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Alice can now share her public key.\n"
msgstr "Alice kini boleh berkongsi kunci awamnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob can now use this to send Alice an encrypted message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bob kini boleh menggunakannya untuk menghantar mesej yang disulitkan kepada "
"Alice.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Bob's message is a single bit.\n"
msgstr "Mesej Bob ialah satu bit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To encrypt the message, Bob needs to select an arbitrary number of samples "
"at random from Alice's public key to form the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyulitkan mesej, Bob perlu memilih bilangan sampel sewenang-"
"wenangnya secara rawak daripada kunci awam Alice untuk membentuk teks "
"sifer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "For this, he creates a mask, a random binary vector $r$ of length $N$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk ini, dia mencipta topeng, vektor binari rawak $r$ dengan panjang "
"$N$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We now take this mask and apply it to the relevant entry in Alice's public "
"key, calculating a sum of the values found.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kini mengambil topeng ini dan menggunakannya pada entri yang berkaitan "
"dalam kunci awam Alice, mengira jumlah nilai yang ditemui.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, Bob broadcasts the ciphertext, which Alice can decrypt using her "
"private key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, Bob menyiarkan teks sifer, yang boleh dinyahsulitkan oleh Alice "
"menggunakan kunci peribadinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since this protocol works bit by bit for encrypting longer bit strings, we "
"simply repeat the operations in a loop. The following shows a scenario where"
" Bob wishes to transfer 16 encrypted bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh kerana protokol ini bekerja bit demi bit untuk menyulitkan rentetan bit"
" yang lebih panjang, kita hanya mengulang operasi dalam gelung. Berikut "
"menunjukkan senario di mana Bob ingin memindahkan 16 bit yang disulitkan.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Module-LWE and the CRYSTALS suite {#module-lwe-and-the-crystals-suite}"
msgstr "Module-LWE dan Suite CRYSTALS {#module-lwe-and-the-crystals-suite}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The learning with errors (LWE) problem, introduced in a simplified form "
"above and generally valid on arbitrary lattices, has been extended to "
"algebraic *rings* within the so-called [**Ring-"
"LWE**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ring_learning_with_errors&oldid=1148731729)"
" framework primarily to improve the efficiency of resulting cryptosystems. "
"However, the extra algebraic structure of Ring-LWE may be potentially "
"exploitable, even though no such exploits are currently known.\n"
msgstr ""
"Masalah pembelajaran dengan ralat (LWE), yang diperkenalkan dalam bentuk "
"ringkas di atas dan secara umum berlaku pada kekisi sembarangan, telah "
"dikembangkan kepada *gelanggang* aljabar dalam rangka kerja yang dikenali "
"sebagai [**Ring-"
"LWE**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ring_learning_with_errors&oldid=1148731729),"
" terutamanya untuk meningkatkan kecekapan sistem kriptografi yang terhasil. "
"Walau bagaimanapun, struktur aljabar tambahan pada Ring-LWE berkemungkinan "
"boleh dieksploitasi, walaupun tiada eksploitasi sedemikian diketahui pada "
"masa ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Two of the four finalists in NIST's QSC standardization process — namely, "
"the [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) key "
"encapsulation mechanism (KEM) and the [**CRYSTALS-Dilithium**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/dilithium/index.shtml) digital signature protocol — are based "
"on structures known as <DefinitionTooltip definition=\"Collection of all "
"submodules of a given module. A submodule is a subset of the module that "
"itself forms a module under the same operations. The set of all submodules "
"forms a lattice, which is a partially ordered set where any two elements "
"have a unique least upper bound and greatest lower bound.\">*module "
"lattices*</DefinitionTooltip> and the related [**Module-"
"LWE**](https://eprint.iacr.org/2012/090).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dua daripada empat finalis dalam proses piawaian QSC NIST — iaitu, mekanisme"
" enkapsulasi kunci (KEM) [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) dan protokol tandatangan digital "
"[**CRYSTALS-Dilithium**](https://pq-crystals.org/dilithium/index.shtml) — "
"adalah berdasarkan struktur yang dikenali sebagai <DefinitionTooltip "
"definition=\"Koleksi semua submodul bagi modul yang diberikan. Submodul "
"ialah subset modul yang sendirinya membentuk modul di bawah operasi yang "
"sama. Set semua submodul membentuk kekisi, iaitu set teratur separa di mana "
"mana-mana dua elemen mempunyai had atas terkecil dan had bawah terbesar yang"
" unik.\">*kekisi modul*</DefinitionTooltip> dan [**Module-"
"LWE**](https://eprint.iacr.org/2012/090) yang berkaitan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We refer interested readers to specialized courses on these topics for the "
"mathematical details but note here that Module-LWE is seen as a compromise "
"between LWE and Ring-LWE. It provides more efficiency than LWE (though less "
"than Ring-LWE) but also gives a higher level of security assurance than "
"Ring-LWE because it does not rely as heavily on the algebraic structure of "
"the problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami merujuk pembaca yang berminat kepada kursus khusus mengenai topik ini "
"untuk mendapatkan butiran matematik, tetapi perlu dinyatakan di sini bahawa "
"Module-LWE dilihat sebagai kompromi antara LWE dan Ring-LWE. Ia memberikan "
"kecekapan yang lebih tinggi daripada LWE (walaupun kurang daripada Ring-LWE)"
" tetapi juga memberikan jaminan keselamatan yang lebih tinggi daripada Ring-"
"LWE kerana ia tidak begitu bergantung pada struktur aljabar masalah "
"tersebut.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Key Encapsulation Mechanisms and CRYSTALS-Kyber {#key-encapsulation-"
"mechanisms-and-crystals-kyber}"
msgstr ""
"Mekanisme Enkapsulasi Kunci dan CRYSTALS-Kyber {#key-encapsulation-"
"mechanisms-and-crystals-kyber}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Traditional asymmetric key cryptosystems are most heavily deployed for their"
" *key-exchange* and *digital signature* functionalities and as such, the "
"NIST standardization process sought to develop quantum-safe alternatives for"
" these two functionalities. The [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) protocol is therefore designed as a "
"dedicated [**Key Encapsulation "
"Mechanism**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" (KEM) rather than as a general purpose encryption scheme such as RSA. A "
"workflow illustrating the use of Kyber to establish a shared secret between "
"two parties is shown below.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem kriptografi kunci asimetrik tradisional paling banyak digunakan untuk"
" fungsi *pertukaran kunci* dan *tandatangan digital*, dan oleh itu, proses "
"piawaian NIST berusaha membangunkan alternatif selamat-kuantum untuk kedua-"
"dua fungsi ini. Protokol [**CRYSTALS-Kyber**](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/kyber/index.shtml) direka bentuk sebagai [**Mekanisme "
"Enkapsulasi "
"Kunci**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Key_encapsulation_mechanism&oldid=1110687965)"
" (KEM) yang khusus dan bukan sebagai skim penyulitan tujuan umum seperti "
"RSA. Aliran kerja yang menggambarkan penggunaan Kyber untuk mewujudkan "
"rahsia dikongsi antara dua pihak ditunjukkan di bawah.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"KEM example using liboqs (local setup required) {#kem-example-using-liboqs-"
"local-setup-required}"
msgstr ""
"Contoh KEM menggunakan liboqs (pemasangan tempatan diperlukan) {#kem-"
"example-using-liboqs-local-setup-required}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"This example requires some additional local installation, and currently cannot be run on this site. You can review the output below, or alternatively copy the cells to a suitable local environment if you wish to run these examples**\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Contoh ini memerlukan beberapa pemasangan tempatan tambahan, dan pada masa ini tidak boleh dijalankan di laman ini. Anda boleh menyemak output di bawah, atau secara alternatif menyalin sel-sel ke persekitaran tempatan yang sesuai jika anda ingin menjalankan contoh-contoh ini**\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here we make use of the algorithms provided by the `liboqs` open source "
"project which provides a libraries for prototyping and experimenting with "
"quantum-safe cryptography. Refer to the links below to setup and test, and "
"then run these examples in your local Python environment.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini kami menggunakan algoritma yang disediakan oleh projek sumber "
"terbuka `liboqs` yang menyediakan pustaka untuk membuat prototaip dan "
"bereksperimen dengan kriptografi selamat-kuantum. Rujuk pautan di bawah "
"untuk pemasangan dan pengujian, kemudian jalankan contoh-contoh ini dalam "
"persekitaran Python tempatan anda.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Python Library:** This provides the Python language binding for liboqs - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs-Python\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pustaka Python:** Ini menyediakan pengikatan bahasa Python untuk liboqs - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs-Python\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**liboqs implementation:** This is required by the Python library, and "
"provides the actual algorithm implementations and must be built - "
"https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/liboqs\n"
msgstr ""
"**Pelaksanaan liboqs:** Ini diperlukan oleh pustaka Python, dan menyediakan "
"pelaksanaan algoritma sebenar serta perlu dibina - https://github.com/open-"
"quantum-safe/liboqs\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice wishes to create and securely communicate a shared secret to Bob using"
" a quantum-safe encryption approach. She will use the `Kyber512` KEM "
"algorithm provided by liboqs.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice ingin mencipta dan menyampaikan rahsia dikongsi kepada Bob dengan "
"selamat menggunakan pendekatan penyulitan selamat-kuantum. Dia akan "
"menggunakan algoritma KEM `Kyber512` yang disediakan oleh liboqs.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We begin by importing relevant Python modules :\n"
msgstr "Kita mulakan dengan mengimport modul Python yang berkaitan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`liboqs` provides a number of KEM implementations and a list of the "
"available algorithms can be easily obtained as follows\n"
msgstr ""
"`liboqs` menyediakan beberapa pelaksanaan KEM dan senarai algoritma yang "
"tersedia boleh diperoleh dengan mudah seperti berikut\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We see that one of the options in the list is `Kyber512` which we will employ in this example. Key exchange using Kyber involves three simple steps namely\n"
"1. Key generation\n"
"2. Encapsulation\n"
"3. Decapsulation\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapati bahawa salah satu pilihan dalam senarai adalah `Kyber512` yang akan kita gunakan dalam contoh ini. Pertukaran kunci menggunakan Kyber melibatkan tiga langkah mudah iaitu\n"
"1. Penjanaan kunci\n"
"2. Enkapsulasi\n"
"3. Dekapsulasi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the key generation step, the recepient Bob, needs to generate an "
"asymmetric key pair using `Kyber512` and broadcast his public key.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam langkah penjanaan kunci, penerima Bob perlu menjana pasangan kunci "
"asimetrik menggunakan `Kyber512` dan menyiarkan kunci awamnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next in the **encapsulation** step, upon receiving Bob's public key, Alice "
"generates both the shared secret and it's corresponding ciphertext using "
"`Kyber512` and Bob's public key. The ciphertext which *encapsulates* the "
"shared secret is then broadcasted to Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seterusnya dalam langkah **enkapsulasi**, setelah menerima kunci awam Bob, "
"Alice menjana kedua-dua rahsia dikongsi dan teks sifer yang sepadan "
"menggunakan `Kyber512` dan kunci awam Bob. Teks sifer yang *mengenkapsulasi*"
" rahsia dikongsi kemudiannya disiarkan kepada Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, in the **decapsulation** step, Bob uses his private key to recover "
"the shared secret from the ciphertext.\n"
msgstr ""
"Akhirnya, dalam langkah **dekapsulasi**, Bob menggunakan kunci peribadi "
"miliknya untuk mendapatkan semula rahsia dikongsi daripada teks sifer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that in contrast to key exchange using RSA, no extraneous padding or "
"key derivation functions are involved here. Kyber's design as a KEM allows "
"for a very minimal user interface while providing the gold standard [**IND-"
"CCA2**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security for key exchange.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perlu diperhatikan bahawa berbeza dengan pertukaran kunci menggunakan RSA, "
"tiada pelapik atau fungsi penurunan kunci yang berlebihan terlibat di sini. "
"Reka bentuk Kyber sebagai KEM membolehkan antara muka pengguna yang sangat "
"minimum sambil memberikan keselamatan piawaian terbaik [**IND-"
"CCA2**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" untuk pertukaran kunci.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"IND-CPA and IND-CCA security in lattice-based cryptography {#ind-cpa-and-"
"ind-cca-security-in-lattice-based-cryptography}"
msgstr ""
"Keselamatan IND-CPA dan IND-CCA dalam kriptografi berasaskan kekisi {#ind-"
"cpa-and-ind-cca-security-in-lattice-based-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the lesson on Symmetric Key Cryptography, we introduced the notion of "
"**semantic security** or **IND-CPA** security which refers to "
"[**indistinguishability under chosen-plaintext "
"attack**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047).\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran mengenai Kriptografi Kunci Simetrik, kami memperkenalkan "
"konsep **keselamatan semantik** atau keselamatan **IND-CPA** yang merujuk "
"kepada [**ketakbolehbezaan di bawah serangan teks biasa "
"terpilih**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Traditional cryptosystems whether symmetric (such as AES) or asymmetric "
"(such as RSA) use deterministic functions to implement encryption "
"operations. This means that a given plaintext, combined with a given "
"encryption key will always encrypt to the same ciphertext. Such "
"deterministic cryptosystems are vulnerable to *chosen plaintext attack* "
"whereby an adversary is able to extract information by requesting "
"encryptions of arbitrary plaintexts of their choice from the deterministic "
"encryption function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem kriptografi tradisional sama ada simetrik (seperti AES) atau "
"asimetrik (seperti RSA) menggunakan fungsi deterministik untuk melaksanakan "
"operasi penyulitan. Ini bermakna teks biasa tertentu, digabungkan dengan "
"kunci penyulitan tertentu, akan sentiasa disulitkan kepada teks sifer yang "
"sama. Sistem kriptografi deterministik sedemikian terdedah kepada *serangan "
"teks biasa terpilih* di mana penyerang dapat mengekstrak maklumat dengan "
"meminta penyulitan teks biasa sembarangan pilihan mereka daripada fungsi "
"penyulitan deterministik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To achieve IND-CPA security in this context, **additional randomness** is "
"introduced at encryption time either through *initialization vectors* or "
"*padding*. For instance AES is only IND-CPA secure when used in [Cipher "
"Block Chaining (CBC) or Gaolis/Counter Mode (GCM) modes of "
"operation](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" that use random initialization vectors. Similarly with RSA, [OAEP "
"padding](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" is need to ensure IND-CPA security.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mencapai keselamatan IND-CPA dalam konteks ini, **kerawakan tambahan**"
" diperkenalkan pada masa penyulitan sama ada melalui *vektor permulaan* atau"
" *pelapik*. Sebagai contoh, AES hanya selamat IND-CPA apabila digunakan "
"dalam [mod operasi Rantaian Blok Sifer (CBC) atau mod Galois/Kaunter "
"(GCM)](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Block_cipher_mode_of_operation&oldid=1154901199#cite_note-23)"
" yang menggunakan vektor permulaan rawak. Begitu juga dengan RSA, [pelapik "
"OAEP](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Optimal_asymmetric_encryption_padding&oldid=1163481577)"
" diperlukan untuk memastikan keselamatan IND-CPA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contrast, lattice-based schemes for encryption are inherently randomized due to the problem definition itself. In particular, in the LWE based encryption scheme outlined above, there are two distinct elements of randomness:\n"
"- **(1)** The error (or noise) $\\varepsilon$ drawn from the distribution $\\chi$\n"
"- **(2)** The random binary vectors $\\mathbf{r} \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$ used for encrypting each bit in the message.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebaliknya, skim berasaskan kekisi untuk penyulitan secara semula jadi dirawakkan disebabkan definisi masalah itu sendiri. Khususnya, dalam skim penyulitan berasaskan LWE yang digariskan di atas, terdapat dua elemen kerawakan yang berbeza:\n"
"- **(1)** Ralat (atau hingar) $\\varepsilon$ yang diambil dari taburan $\\chi$\n"
"- **(2)** Vektor binari rawak $\\mathbf{r} \\in \\{0,1\\}^N$ yang digunakan untuk menyulitkan setiap bit dalam mesej.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The errors $\\varepsilon$ contribute to the security of the public key, "
"ensuring that it's computationally hard to deduce the secret key "
"$\\mathbf{s}$. The random binary vectors $\\mathbf{r}$ on the other hand "
"provide the essential randomness needed for making repeated encryptions of "
"the same plaintext bit non-deterministic. Thus LWE based schemes are "
"considered IND-CPA secure without the need for external mechanisms such as "
"padding.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ralat $\\varepsilon$ menyumbang kepada keselamatan kunci awam, memastikan "
"bahawa secara pengkomputeran ia sukar untuk mendeduksi kunci rahsia "
"$\\mathbf{s}$. Vektor binari rawak $\\mathbf{r}$ pula memberikan kerawakan "
"penting yang diperlukan untuk menjadikan penyulitan berulang bagi bit teks "
"biasa yang sama tidak deterministik. Oleh itu, skim berasaskan LWE dianggap "
"selamat IND-CPA tanpa memerlukan mekanisme luaran seperti pelapik.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Modern cryptosystems aim to achieve so called [**IND-"
"CCA**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" security which stands for **indistinguishability under chosen-ciphertext "
"attack**. In this setting the adversary has the ability to obtain "
"decryptions of a non-trival set of ciphertexts of their choosing with the "
"aim of extracting information to subsequently break the cryptosystem. A "
"scheme is IND-CCA secure if, even with this capability, the adversary cannot"
" do better than random guessing when trying to distinguish encrypted "
"messages. IND-CCA is a stronger security notion than IND-CPA and subsumes "
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem kriptografi moden bertujuan untuk mencapai keselamatan [**IND-"
"CCA**](https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Ciphertext_indistinguishability&oldid=1130147047)"
" yang disebut, yang bermaksud **ketakbolehbezaan di bawah serangan teks "
"sifer terpilih**. Dalam tetapan ini, penyerang mempunyai keupayaan untuk "
"mendapatkan penyahsulitan set teks sifer bukan trivial pilihan mereka dengan"
" tujuan mengekstrak maklumat untuk seterusnya memecahkan sistem kriptografi."
" Satu skim adalah selamat IND-CCA jika, walaupun dengan keupayaan ini, "
"penyerang tidak dapat melakukan lebih baik daripada meneka secara rawak "
"apabila cuba membezakan mesej yang disulitkan. IND-CCA adalah konsep "
"keselamatan yang lebih kuat daripada IND-CPA dan merangkuminya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum safe KEMs such as **Kyber** are designed to be IND-CCA secure. This is achieved in two steps:\n"
"1. An IND-CPA secure public key encryption(PKE) scheme is defined. In the case of Kyber such a PKE is based on **Module-LWE**.\n"
"2. A variant of the [Fujisaki-Okamoto transform](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1) (FO) is applied to obtain a CCA-secure KEM. The FO transformation is a generic method to convert encryption schemes that are IND-CPA secure into ones that are IND-CCA secure. For details we refer readers to the [original papers](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1).\n"
msgstr ""
"KEM selamat-kuantum seperti **Kyber** direka bentuk untuk selamat IND-CCA. Ini dicapai dalam dua langkah:\n"
"1. Skim penyulitan kunci awam (PKE) yang selamat IND-CPA ditakrifkan. Dalam kes Kyber, PKE sedemikian adalah berdasarkan **Module-LWE**.\n"
"2. Varian [transformasi Fujisaki-Okamoto](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1) (FO) digunakan untuk mendapatkan KEM yang selamat CCA. Transformasi FO adalah kaedah generik untuk menukar skim penyulitan yang selamat IND-CPA kepada skim yang selamat IND-CCA. Untuk butiran, kami merujuk pembaca kepada [makalah asal](https://doi.org/10.1007/s00145-011-9114-1).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For more information on the security features of **Kyber** and "
"**Dilithium**, as well as reference implementations in various programming "
"languages, you are encouraged to consult the [CRYSTALS suite "
"documentation](https://pq-crystals.org/).\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk maklumat lanjut mengenai ciri keselamatan **Kyber** dan **Dilithium**,"
" serta pelaksanaan rujukan dalam pelbagai bahasa pengaturcaraan, anda "
"digalakkan untuk merujuk [dokumentasi suite CRYSTALS](https://pq-"
"crystals.org/).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Hybrid cryptography {#hybrid-cryptography}"
msgstr "Kriptografi hibrid {#hybrid-cryptography}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Hybrid cryptography refers to using quantum-safe public-key algorithms are "
"combined with traditional public key algorithms (like RSA or elliptic "
"curves) such that the solution is at least no less secure than existing "
"traditional cryptography.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kriptografi hibrid merujuk kepada penggunaan algoritma kunci awam selamat-"
"kuantum yang digabungkan dengan algoritma kunci awam tradisional (seperti "
"RSA atau lengkung elips) supaya penyelesaian tersebut sekurang-kurangnya "
"tidak kurang selamat daripada kriptografi tradisional sedia ada.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This can help address 2 issues:\n"
msgstr "Ini boleh membantu menangani 2 isu:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Existing standards may mandate specific algorithms to be used for "
"encryption, or that such algorithms are in some way approved. To add quantum"
" safety, encryption could first be done using the regular algorithm, but "
"then further protected by a quantum-safe algorithm, whilst still meeting "
"required standards.\n"
msgstr ""
"Piawaian sedia ada mungkin menetapkan algoritma tertentu untuk digunakan "
"bagi penyulitan, atau bahawa algoritma tersebut diluluskan dalam sesuatu "
"cara. Untuk menambah keselamatan kuantum, penyulitan boleh dilakukan "
"terlebih dahulu menggunakan algoritma biasa, tetapi kemudian dilindungi "
"lebih lanjut oleh algoritma selamat-kuantum, sambil masih memenuhi piawaian "
"yang diperlukan.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum algorithms are new, and further analysis is needed to ensure they "
"are indeed safe and correct. For example one of the initial algorithms "
"shortlisted by NIST was subsequently cracked and proven to be insecure. To "
"mitigate this risk, encryption can be done both using a standard, well-"
"reviewed, secure (apart from quantum!) algorithm, in addition to a post-"
"quantum algorithm.\n"
msgstr ""
"Algoritma kuantum adalah baharu, dan analisis lanjut diperlukan untuk "
"memastikan ia memang selamat dan betul. Sebagai contoh, salah satu algoritma"
" awal yang disenaraipendekkan oleh NIST kemudiannya dipecahkan dan terbukti "
"tidak selamat. Untuk mengurangkan risiko ini, penyulitan boleh dilakukan "
"menggunakan algoritma standard yang telah dikaji semula dengan teliti dan "
"selamat (selain daripada kuantum!), selain daripada algoritma pasca-"
"kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Summary {#summary}"
msgstr "Ringkasan {#summary}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The migration to quantum-safe cryptography (QSC) of asymmetric key "
"cryptosystems is necessitated by the expected advent of quantum computers "
"that can break traditional asymmetric key algorithms predicated on the "
"classical hardness of NP-intermediate problems. QSC is conjectured to be "
"robust to quantum attacks because its security is based on NP-hard problems,"
" which generally cannot be efficiently solved even with quantum computers.\n"
msgstr ""
"Penghijrahan kepada kriptografi selamat-kuantum (QSC) bagi sistem "
"kriptografi kunci asimetrik diperlukan oleh kemunculan yang dijangka bagi "
"komputer kuantum yang boleh memecahkan algoritma kunci asimetrik tradisional"
" yang bergantung pada kesukaran klasik masalah NP-perantaraan. QSC dijangka "
"tahan terhadap serangan kuantum kerana keselamatannya adalah berdasarkan "
"masalah NP-sukar, yang secara umumnya tidak dapat diselesaikan dengan cekap "
"walaupun dengan komputer kuantum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this context, hard problems rooted in the theory of mathematical lattices"
" such as the learning with errors (LWE) problem have emerged as leading "
"contenders for QSC standardization. In particular, the CRYSTALS-Kyber and "
"CRYSTALS-Dilithium algorithms, based on modular lattices, are well "
"positioned as near-term alternatives to popular asymmetric key protocols "
"like RSA, Elliptic Curve, Diffie-Hellman, and DSA.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam konteks ini, masalah sukar yang berakar umbi dalam teori kekisi "
"matematik seperti masalah pembelajaran dengan ralat (LWE) telah muncul "
"sebagai calon utama untuk piawaian QSC. Khususnya, algoritma CRYSTALS-Kyber "
"dan CRYSTALS-Dilithium, berdasarkan kekisi modular, berada dalam kedudukan "
"yang baik sebagai alternatif jangka pendek kepada protokol kunci asimetrik "
"popular seperti RSA, Lengkung Elips, Diffie-Hellman, dan DSA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we navigate the complex landscape of quantum-safe cryptography, embracing"
" these innovative solutions will be pivotal in upholding the integrity and "
"confidentiality of our digital interactions in the quantum era.\n"
msgstr ""
"Semasa kita mengemudi landskap kriptografi selamat-kuantum yang kompleks, "
"merangkul penyelesaian inovatif ini akan menjadi penting dalam "
"mempertahankan integriti dan kerahsiaan interaksi digital kita di era "
"kuantum.\n"
